W("Examine the structure of the poem: how do the first and second halves differ?", 4, "The first four lines deal with fire (the opinions and the poet's choice). The last five turn with 'But' to ice and an argument that it too could end the world. The same rhymes recur at both ends, so the poem returns to its start like a closed circle. (4)", "H"),
W("The poem has no proper nouns, no description of landscape and no characters. How does this help it?", 3, "The absence of concrete details makes the idea universal and timeless; it applies to any person or age. The focus stays on the symbols. (3)", "H"),
