W("Why is the poet's use of 'tasted' a good choice of word? Link it with the theme.", 3, "'Tasted' makes desire a bodily experience, like food; it suggests personal knowledge and also that desire is something one can crave. It supports the first-person speaker. (3)", "H"),
W("Explain how sound and rhythm help the idea of the poem. Refer to rhyme and line length.", 4, "Short and long lines are mixed, as if thought pauses and rushes. The repeated rhymes (fire/desire/fire; ice/twice/ice/suffice) tie the poem together and echo like a warning. The last short lines 'Is also great / And would suffice' close in quick, cold finality. (4)", "H"),
